        "text": "*[Bug 18960] tools::undoc(dir=) errors unless dir=\".\" in the presence of Rd with \\packageDescription macro*\n<https:\/\/bugs.r-project.org\/show_bug.cgi?id=18960>\n\n--- Comment #3 from Michael Chirico (<mailto:michaelchirico4@gmail.com|michaelchirico4@gmail.com>) ---\nCreated attachment 3798\n  --&gt; <https:\/\/bugs.r-project.org\/attachment.cgi?id=3798&amp;action=edit>\nFix Rd_macros_package_dir() to read from processRdChunk_data_store()\n\nIncluding a [tested](<https:\/\/github.com\/r-devel\/r-svn\/pull\/305>) patch in\nservice of the above with which I am reasonably happy as it obviates some\n'UGLY! FIXME' comments.\n\nSince those comments were written, `processRdChunk_data_store()` was added\n(r88497) which looks like it was intended for cases like bug under\nconsideration. This allows `prepare_Rd()` (and friends) to reconstruct the\npackage directory instead of managing state with `env`.\n\nDisclosure: this work was heavily assisted by LLM, which found\n`processRdChunk_data_store()` at my repeated insistence that an earlier\nsuggestion with `_R_RD_MACROS_PACKAGE_DIR_` was just too ugly, and which wrote\nthe original outline of the tests (since stylized).",
        "username": "r-bugs notifier",
        "icons": {
