                                "type": "link",
                                "url": "https:\/\/github.com\/r-devel\/r-svn\/pull\/305"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": ") patch in\nservice of the above with which I am reasonably happy as it obviates some\n'UGLY! FIXME' comments.\n\nSince those comments were written, "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "processRdChunk_data_store()",
                                "style": {
                                    "code": true
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " was added\n(r88497) which looks like it was intended for cases like bug under\nconsideration. This allows "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "prepare_Rd()",
                                "style": {
                                    "code": true
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " (and friends) to reconstruct the\npackage directory instead of managing state with "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "env",
                                "style": {
                                    "code": true
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": ".\n\nDisclosure: this work was heavily assisted by LLM, which found\n"
                            },
